# The KosmicKrisp driver, pinned. fetch-driver.sh verifies the downloaded asset
# against this and refuses anything else, so this file -- not the rolling
# `latest` tag -- is what makes the fetch reproducible.
#
# Bumping the driver is two steps and the second is not optional: upload the new
# dylib to the release (vendor-kosmickrisp.sh prints the command), then commit
# the new hash here. Until that commit lands every fetch fails on the mismatch,
# which is the intended failure -- the alternative is shipping a driver nobody
# chose.
#
# mesa 26.3.0-devel
c98d6fffd38478ece406fb6bb359aedf4b4a8efe86f1345e963a5a9c23393ad5  libvulkan_kosmickrisp.dylib
